      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lincoln%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Renamed after President Abraham Lincoln, the city became Nebraska's state capital in 1869.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lincoln%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The University of Nebraska, founded in Lincoln in 1869, remains the state's flagship institution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lincoln%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The MoPac Trail stretches 27 miles from UNL’s campus eastward to Wabash, tracing a former Missouri Pacific Railroad line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
